# Creating and Using Functions in JavaScript

Images need to be changed from python - lb isn't loading images right now :cry:

#### Now that we know why functions are useful, let’s look at how to make one in JavaScript.

#### There are a few key steps:

## 🧩 **1. Give your function a name**
#### A function needs a name so you can refer to it later. Pick something that describes what the function does, like `showMessage` or `calculate_total`.
#### *Remember in JavaScript we usually use camelCase for function names (like `addScore` or `changeColor`).
---



## 🔧 **2. Use the function keyword to define the function**
#### In JavaScript, a basic function starts with the word **function**, followed by the function’s name and parentheses `()` and curly braces `{}`.

#### The curly braces hold the code that will run when the function is called.

<img src="https://images.code.org/d1d4d3a51160578261fa58167815c8c4-image-1745423539641.png" alt="Python code defining a function reading def greet" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0 0 40px 10px;">

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

## 🧱 **3. Write the code you want to run (inside the braces)**
#### The code inside the braces `{}` runs each time a function is called. 
#### You can put one line or many lines of code inside your function. 

<img src="https://images.code.org/f79184f8c12b563c740ec65b67acd854-image-1745423616328.png" alt="Python code defining a function reading def greet with an indented print statement saying hello world" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0 0 40px 10px;">

<div style="clear:both;"></div>


---

## ▶️ **4. Call the function to make it run**
#### Just defining a function doesn’t run it. You have to call it by typing its name with parentheses:

<img src="https://images.code.org/17f108b4e01f652c36a3c379d85c948f-image-1745424413545.png" alt="Python code defining a function reading def greet with an indented print statement saying hello world and then the function greet being called" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0 0 40px 10px;">

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

## Next up
#### You’ll see how to write the same kind of function using arrow function syntax — a shorter, modern way to define functions in JavaScript.


MARKDOWN
